**Report date:** 07 Aug 2026
**Source:** Google Search Console → Page Indexing → "Why pages aren't indexed" → Soft 404
**Status in GSC:** Validation **Failed** (validation attempt started 14 Jun 2026, failed 25 Jul 2026)
**Affected pages:** 82
**Last data point:** 24 Jul 2026

---

## 1. What "Soft 404" means

Google crawled these URLs, got an HTTP 200 (success) response, but the _content_ of the page looked empty, broken, or non-existent — so Google treats it the same as a 404 and refuses to index it. This is a content/template issue, not a server-error issue (`Server error (5xx)` in the same report shows 0 pages).

Typical causes: an empty results list, a "no data found" message with no other content, a template that renders near-identically for every URL in the group, or extremely thin unique content per page.

